e/14040011/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-281030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(-1,0,1),$ $B(2,-3,4),$ $C(-2,-2,2),$ and $D(0,-1,5).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd388d00a70ed291b41e763546f24dc223c781c7cc6900097248a4b716cf78ea" "basis" 1398 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-281030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i-3j+4k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =3i-3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨3,-3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2i-2j+2k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =-i-2j+1k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(-j+5k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =i-j+4k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|-(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(-8+1)+3(-4-1)+3(1-(-2)) \\\\  & =-21-15+9 \\\\  & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-27|=27.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd388d00a70ed291b41e763546f24dc223c781c7cc6900097248a4b716cf78ea" "basis" 1398 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-281030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f1eb67db518936ec2db7e8202c1597822f37f8d6e6f051fdbf9470bb1bc3f378" "basis" 1398 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-281030" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd388d00a70ed291b41e763546f24dc223c781c7cc6900097248a4b716cf78ea" "basis" 1398 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-281030" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "27"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/state.json" "file_sha256" "bd388d00a70ed291b41e763546f24dc223c781c7cc6900097248a4b716cf78ea" "basis" 1398 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-4,2 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,-2,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,0,3 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/example-4350.json" "file_sha256" "586799041ff3e08eb8ad0af1ea5303ee47b721102cfdddf503e7f78f3946a0d3" "basis" 1398 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0)+4(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1))+2(0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-6+4-4 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV = |-6| = 6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/example-4350.json" "file_sha256" "586799041ff3e08eb8ad0af1ea5303ee47b721102cfdddf503e7f78f3946a0d3" "basis" 1398 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $k$ given that the vectors $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle k,2,1 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -2,-1,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,1,2 \\rangle$ are coplanar." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/example-4351.json" "file_sha256" "aaf511d232f4dcc97de3dab904c9507b208301e2678ae5c00c325b4f58a7a7b7" "basis" 1398 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(-1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)-2(-2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1)+(-2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-3k+6-3 \\\\  & =-3k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ -3k+3 & =0 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=1$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/example-4351.json" "file_sha256" "aaf511d232f4dcc97de3dab904c9507b208301e2678ae5c00c325b4f58a7a7b7" "basis" 1398 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD},$ given the points $A(3,-1,2),$ $B(2,1,1),$ $C(-1,2,1),$ and $D(4,4,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/example-4352.json" "file_sha256" "fb48d45a8e3b284975c75b39d6c82156810e55342147290d26b931e3ee83bd05" "basis" 1398 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+2j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-4i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-4,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(4i+4j+2k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =i+5j \\\\  & =⟨1,5,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(3\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-1))-2((-4)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1))-((-4)\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-5-2+23 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|16|=16.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/example-4352.json" "file_sha256" "fb48d45a8e3b284975c75b39d6c82156810e55342147290d26b931e3ee83bd05" "basis" 1398 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040011/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-18259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨-3,3,1⟩$, $b=⟨2,-1,3⟩$ and $c=⟨0,4,1⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-18259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3((-1)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 3)-3(2\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 3)+(2\\cdot 4-0\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =39-6+8 \\\\  & =41\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|41|=41.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-18259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087550a9341b0a6af05c3359fe96ecca59d533f1efe1c77e017047356a89ffc0"} {"question" "q-18259" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-18259" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "15"] ["math" "32"] ["math" "35"] ["math" "41"] ["math" "53"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-18259" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "41"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-42050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨1,-2,1⟩$, $b=⟨2,-4,1⟩$ and $c=⟨0,2,5⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-42050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 1)+2(2\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 1)+(2\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-4)) \\\\  & =-22+20+4 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|2|=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-42050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087550a9341b0a6af05c3359fe96ecca59d533f1efe1c77e017047356a89ffc0"} {"question" "q-42050" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-42050" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-42050" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-280670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $x=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $y=⟨0,1,-1⟩$, and $z=⟨2,0,1⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-280670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)-2(0\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 2)+3(0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =1-4-6 \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-9|=9.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-280670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087550a9341b0a6af05c3359fe96ecca59d533f1efe1c77e017047356a89ffc0"} {"question" "q-280670" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-280670" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-40221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨-5,3,0⟩$, $b=⟨2,-1,4⟩$ and $c=⟨1,1,1⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-40221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-5((-1)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 4)-3(2\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 4)+0 \\\\  & =25+6 \\\\  & =31\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|31|=31.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-40221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087550a9341b0a6af05c3359fe96ecca59d533f1efe1c77e017047356a89ffc0"} {"question" "q-40221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-40221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "16"] ["math" "22"] ["math" "31"] ["math" "32"] ["math" "59"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-40221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "31"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-128421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $p=⟨2,2,3⟩,$ $q=⟨4,2,-1⟩,$ and $r=⟨-5,0,3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-128421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(2\\cdot 3-0\\cdot (-1))-2(4\\cdot 3-(-5)\\cdot (-1))+3(4\\cdot 0-(-5)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =12-14+30 \\\\  & =28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|28|=28.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-128421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087550a9341b0a6af05c3359fe96ecca59d533f1efe1c77e017047356a89ffc0"} {"question" "q-128421" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-128421" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "14"] ["math" "28"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "42"] ["math" "56"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-128421" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "28"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-128436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨k,1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨8,0,3⟩,$ and $c=⟨3,1,1⟩$ are coplanar." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-128436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(0\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 3)-(8\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 3)+4(8\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-3k+1+32 \\\\  & =33-3k \\\\  & =3(11-k).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 3(11-k) & =0 \\\\ 11-k & =0 \\\\ k & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=11.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-128436" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087550a9341b0a6af05c3359fe96ecca59d533f1efe1c77e017047356a89ffc0"} {"question" "q-128436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-128436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{11}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{14}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-128436" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-280722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨1,3,0⟩$, $b=⟨0,4,2⟩$, and $c=⟨2,k,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-280722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\na\\cdot (b\\times c)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k & 5\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ k & 5\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 5-2\\cdot k)-3(0\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 2)=(20-2k)+12 \\\\  & =32-2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 32-2k & =0 \\\\ -2k & =-32 \\\\ k & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=16.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-280722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087550a9341b0a6af05c3359fe96ecca59d533f1efe1c77e017047356a89ffc0"} {"question" "q-280722" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-280722" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "16"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-280720" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $k$ given that the vectors $x=⟨2,0,k⟩$, $y=⟨1,4,3⟩$, and $z=⟨0,2,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-280720" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & k \\\\ 1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|+k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(4\\cdot 5-3\\cdot 2)+0+k(1\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =2(20-6)+2k \\\\  & =28+2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =0 \\\\ 28+2k & =0 \\\\ 2k & =-28 \\\\ k & =-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-14.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-280720" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087550a9341b0a6af05c3359fe96ecca59d533f1efe1c77e017047356a89ffc0"} {"question" "q-280720" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-280720" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-14"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-275353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨-2,1,-3⟩$, $b=⟨-1,k,2⟩$, and $c=⟨3,-2,4⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-275353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & k & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|+(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & k \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2(k\\cdot 4-(-2)\\cdot 2)-((-1)\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 2)-3((-1)\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot k) \\\\  & =-8k-8+10-6+9k \\\\  & =k-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ k-4 & =0 \\\\ k & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-275353" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087550a9341b0a6af05c3359fe96ecca59d533f1efe1c77e017047356a89ffc0"} {"question" "q-275353" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-275353" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-42048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨k,2,2⟩$, $b=⟨3,0,2⟩$ and $c=⟨4,1,3⟩$ are coplanar." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-42048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 2)-2(3\\cdot 3-4\\cdot 2)+2(3\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-2k-2+6 \\\\  & =-2k+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ -2k+4 & =0 \\\\ 2k & =4 \\\\ k & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-42048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087550a9341b0a6af05c3359fe96ecca59d533f1efe1c77e017047356a89ffc0"} {"question" "q-42048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-42048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "k=-2"] ["math" "k=-6"] ["math" "k=2"] ["math" "k=3"] ["math" "k=6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-42048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k=2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-73746" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(0,1,2)$, $B(-1,0,1)$, $C(1,1,0)$, and $D(3,-1,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-73746" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-i+k)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =-i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+j)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =i-2k \\\\  & =⟨1,0,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i-j+3k)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =3i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot (-2))+(1\\cdot 1-3\\cdot (-2))-(1\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =4+7+2 \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|13|=13.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-73746" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087550a9341b0a6af05c3359fe96ecca59d533f1efe1c77e017047356a89ffc0"} {"question" "q-73746" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-73746" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11"] ["math" "13"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "20"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-73746" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "13"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-73753" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(-2,1,1)$, $B(2,1,0)$, $C(1,-1,2)$, and $D(3,-2,-2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-73753" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+j)-(-2i+j+k) \\\\  & =4i-k \\\\  & =⟨4,0,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i-j+2k)-(-2i+j+k) \\\\  & =3i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i-2j-2k)-(-2i+j+k) \\\\  & =5i-3j-3k \\\\  & =⟨5,-3,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -3\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4((-2)\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot (-3))-0-(3\\cdot (-3)-5\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =36-1 \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|35|=35.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-73753" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087550a9341b0a6af05c3359fe96ecca59d533f1efe1c77e017047356a89ffc0"} {"question" "q-73753" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-73753" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "27"] ["math" "35"] ["math" "37"] ["math" "40"] ["math" "42"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-73753" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "35"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-281030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(-1,0,1),$ $B(2,-3,4),$ $C(-2,-2,2),$ and $D(0,-1,5).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-281030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i-3j+4k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =3i-3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨3,-3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2i-2j+2k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =-i-2j+1k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(-j+5k)-(-i+1k) \\\\  & =i-j+4k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|-(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(-8+1)+3(-4-1)+3(1-(-2)) \\\\  & =-21-15+9 \\\\  & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-27|=27.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-281030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087550a9341b0a6af05c3359fe96ecca59d533f1efe1c77e017047356a89ffc0"} {"question" "q-281030" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-281030" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "27"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-73744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(1,1,0)$, $B(-2,1,0)$, $C(3,2,0)$, and $D(1,2,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-73744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2i+j)-(i+j) \\\\  & =-3i \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(3i+2j)-(i+j) \\\\  & =2i+1j \\\\  & =⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(i+2j+3k)-(i+j) \\\\  & =3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0)-0+0 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-9|=9.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-73744" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087550a9341b0a6af05c3359fe96ecca59d533f1efe1c77e017047356a89ffc0"} {"question" "q-73744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-73744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-73744" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-281025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(3,0,2),$ $B(5,1,3),$ $C(4,3,5),$ and $D(3,0,5).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-281025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(5i+1j+3k)-(3i+2k) \\\\  & =2i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(4i+3j+5k)-(3i+2k) \\\\  & =i+3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨1,3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i+5k)-(3i+2k) \\\\  & =3k \\\\  & =⟨0,0,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(3\\cdot 3-3\\cdot 0)-1(1\\cdot 3-3\\cdot 0)+1(1\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =2(9)-1(3)+1(0) \\\\  & =18-3+0 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|15|=15.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-281025" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "087550a9341b0a6af05c3359fe96ecca59d533f1efe1c77e017047356a89ffc0"} {"question" "q-281025" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "q-281025" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/state.json" "file_sha256" "1fd6b6b19182000181a0565afab1a243a5ccee3fc82e98593bd1706e87e19411"} {"question" "e-4350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 1,-4,2 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,-2,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,0,3 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/example-4350.json" "file_sha256" "d688918cd9461d7134ffe402f212b7d59a4291a17e38f3b7361ef5555ca4409e"} {"question" "e-4350" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-4)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0)+4(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1))+2(0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-6+4-4 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV = |-6| = 6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/example-4350.json" "file_sha256" "d688918cd9461d7134ffe402f212b7d59a4291a17e38f3b7361ef5555ca4409e"} {"question" "e-4351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $k$ given that the vectors $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle k,2,1 \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -2,-1,1 \\rangle,$ and $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle -1,1,2 \\rangle$ are coplanar." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/example-4351.json" "file_sha256" "3796668eeaf9c3b5b81d9ac0a853b52cc96a6c238e2f2cd1d67c196285cacf4c"} {"question" "e-4351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(-1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)-2(-2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1)+(-2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-3k+6-3 \\\\  & =-3k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ -3k+3 & =0 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=1$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/example-4351.json" "file_sha256" "3796668eeaf9c3b5b81d9ac0a853b52cc96a6c238e2f2cd1d67c196285cacf4c"} {"question" "e-4352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD},$ given the points $A(3,-1,2),$ $B(2,1,1),$ $C(-1,2,1),$ and $D(4,4,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/example-4352.json" "file_sha256" "2a44493272926c7bcbfda20c22e81da58ca517034c60b11ec93cd4049cb41e31"} {"question" "e-4352" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+2j+k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-4i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-4,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(4i+4j+2k)-(3i-j+2k) \\\\  & =i+5j \\\\  & =⟨1,5,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(3\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-1))-2((-4)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1))-((-4)\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-5-2+23 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB},$ $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|16|=16.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14047596/example-4352.json" "file_sha256" "2a44493272926c7bcbfda20c22e81da58ca517034c60b11ec93cd4049cb41e31"}] "usage" {"e-4350" [] "e-4351" [] "e-4352" [] "q-128436" [] "q-280670" [] "q-281030" []} "basis" 1698 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186304797 17592186304798 17592186304799 17592186304800 17592186304801 17592186304832 17592186304833 17592186304851] "immutable_fields" [[17592186304796 :answer-field/correct] [17592186304796 :answer-field/id] [17592186304796 :answer-field/key] [17592186304796 :answer-field/type] [17592186304831 :answer-field/correct] [17592186304831 :answer-field/id] [17592186304831 :answer-field/key] [17592186304831 :answer-field/type] [17592186304850 :answer-field/correct] [17592186304850 :answer-field/id] [17592186304850 :answer-field/key] [17592186304850 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
